package frontend

templ API() {
	<div style="max-width: 700px;margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;">
		<p>
			This page describes the public HTTP API of War Thunder Heatmaps. The API is free.
			To get access feel free to contact me to get your key. Provide it in
			<code>Authorization</code> request header. The data covers ground to ground kills in realistic battles only.
			If you want another view of the data, or images, read the
			<a href="/about">About</a> page and contact me.
		</p>
		<div>
			<h3>GET /api/v1/region</h3>
			<p>
				Returns kill and death counts for top n vehicles by sample count.
				The box is given as fractions of the tank map, from 0 to 1.
				<code>u</code> is the horizontal axis and <code>v</code> is the vertical axis.
				This is effectively identical to frontend area select table.
			</p>
			<p>
				Query parameters:
				<ul>
					<li><code>level</code> (needed) map file name, for example <code>levels/avg_abandoned_town.bin</code>. The map selector on the main page uses the same values.</li>
					<li><code>u0</code>, <code>v0</code>, <code>u1</code>, <code>v1</code> (needed) the two corners of the box</li>
					<li>General kill query params as per frontend form, see them with dev tools or in frontend.templ sources</li>
				</ul>
			</p>
			<p>
				The answer is a JSON array. Each element has these fields:
				<ul>
					<li><code>vehicle</code> internal vehicle name</li>
					<li><code>kills</code> number of kills made by that vehicle in the box</li>
					<li><code>deaths</code> number of deaths of that vehicle in the box</li>
				</ul>
			</p>
			<p>
				Status codes:
				<ul>
					<li><code>200</code> the answer is in the body</li>
					<li><code>204</code> the map is not known</li>
					<li><code>400</code> a needed parameter is missing or malformed</li>
					<li><code>500</code> something broke, let me know about it</li>
				</ul>
			</p>
			<p>
				Example:
				<br/>
				<code>
					curl 'https://thunder.nanachi.party/api/v1/region?level=levels/avg_abandoned_town.bin&amp;u0=0.1&amp;v0=0.1&amp;u1=0.4&amp;v1=0.4'
					-H 'Authorization: Bearer a6706829ad43513107f564c7c69c18e993ead10d34423d7e23e67027d87d2175'
				</code>
			</p>
		</div>
		<div>
			<h3>GET /api/v1/ingestPreferences</h3>
			<p>
				Returns ingest preferences in the ingest provider spec.
				Designed for ingest-sharing by appending it to your own preferences.
				<br/>
				This endpoint does not require Authorization header.
			</p>
		</div>
		<div>
			<h3>GET /api/v1/posStat</h3>
			<p>
				Provides a position summary: it's raw sample count for kills and deaths with
				additional azimuths for entries where position with a victim or a killer. Collected data is
				from 3x3 meter area centered on specified point.
			</p>
			<p>
				Query parameters:
				<ul>
					<li><code>level</code> same as /region</li>
					<li><code>x</code>, <code>z</code> integer coordinates of the position, from level origin (not tankmap, level itself)</li>
				</ul>
			</p>
			<p>
				Reply:
				<pre>
					{ `{
  "angles": {
    "deathsFrom": "Angle,Count;32,5;349,3;284,3;33,3;31,3;282,3;34,3;",
    "toKills": "Angle,Count;283,20;284,16;347,12;349,10;286,10;32,9;282,9;30,7;350,6;33,6;36,5;"
  },
  "tally": {
    "deaths": 61,
    "kills": 190
  }
}` }
				</pre>
				<p>
					Angles are formatted in degrees as a ; separated rows with first one being the header.
				</p>
			</p>
			<p>
				Example:
				<br/>
				<code>
					curl 'https://thunder.nanachi.party/api/v1/posStat?level=levels%2Favg_mozdok.bin&x=2222&z=2273'
					-H 'Authorization: Bearer a6706829ad43513107f564c7c69c18e993ead10d34423d7e23e67027d87d2175'
				</code>
			</p>
		</div>
	</div>
}
